{"title":"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The five-digit positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a73e9c5215030435b1430899a18c5df5d33d22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15AB9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is a perfect square for some digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf77c6740d00af2866f26718d628a60c667ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />? \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the integer must be a square of a number greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c2503e7c421830231e80865ed10e16be2ae2b84d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^{2} = 14400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" />, which would be less than the number. However, we also realize that it must be the square of a number less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed053c218042da5437116773b5ec17ac57d8a4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$130$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/88590e267bc555857caa38f517c32ce3763ac5f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$130^{2} = 16900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" />, which is greater than the number wanted.\n</p><p>We also realize that the units digit must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/3/cd32c9bea9ffacbf413f1030293c9a8091c4e4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{2} = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24acc458ce27972d20b1349d2eb9d8ae77b3d9b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^{2} = 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, which both end in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, like the positive integer we want. \n</p><p>Combining this, the number must be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04b867ea2881ba89a7f5489ffab931af2e59e1c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$123^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c90341c51982ca8adaf19b1fe1a366a9f6556fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$127^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f1c40420211ab630ab25c831cebee7efe049492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$123^{2} = (120 + 3)^{2} = 120^{2} + 2 \\times 120 \\times 3 + 3^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f28230f715eb8b51c49fb6c75be15a9b1f9548fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=14400 + 720 + 9 = 15129$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"217\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We can see that this matches our number, and we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a73e9c5215030435b1430899a18c5df5d33d22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15AB9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c8043fa4178c60c62554fa34b1e0a8f87e0e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15129$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da3d600d21b2b1343040ecb85db0e354a60e96a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed45766ae06d282b582b4b49d4289dcc81331314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = 2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf5e52cd2de714b0c787c943aa958de7a4265753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B = 1 + 2 = \\boxed{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"162\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC\">2014 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 1\">Individual Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 3\">Individual Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 1\">Individual 1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Individual 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 3\">Individual 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 4\">Individual 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Individual 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CE